query_cache: the ranges of a query sync stay inside a 64 KiB page of the buffer cache

Run 53 (Ocarina) ended in BufferCache::CreateBuffer below ObtainCPUBuffer in SyncValues, refused
10,027,008 bytes with 1 MiB left in the pool's largest block. A query writes 8 bytes. SyncValues
joins neighbouring 4 KiB pages into one range, also across a 64 KiB page of the buffer cache, and
FindBuffer on a range half in a buffer makes a new buffer for all of that buffer, 8 MiB more when
its stream score has passed the mark. The new one has to come out of a pool that has nothing left.

Pages now join only inside one 64 KiB page. Such a range is in a buffer already, since buffers cover
whole pages, or asks for 64 KiB, which fits the holes. Cost: one more copy region per 64 KiB. Memory:
10 MiB less at the worst moment.

Proven from the source: a range inside one page never reaches JoinOverlap (ResolveOverlaps walks
only that page). Likely: that the 10 MiB of run 53 was such a join; the log has the size and not the
range. Stands alone. Not built or run on a console.

Sources: runs 51-53 of 2026-11-05, the stream leap in BufferCache::ResolveOverlaps (yuzu).

